// ControlledByYou = the generic "<X> you control" filter shape (the
// controller-restriction idiom behind anthem effects and the general
// "you control" postnominal restriction): wraps any base quality
// `Param(0)` with the controller-is-you relation,
// mirroring the already-lexicalized `OtherCreatureYouControl`/
// `CreatureOpponentControls` siblings (`body: And([Creature, ...
// ControlledBy(...)])`) but parameterized over the base predicate instead of
// fixing it to `Creature`. Body verified against real constructors, not
// taken on trust: `Predicate::And(Arc<[Predicate]>)`
// (`crates/deckmaste_core/src/filter.rs:192`, `cargo xtask map enums`) and
// `RelationPredicate::ControlledBy(Arc<Predicate>)` (`filter.rs:146`), the
// exact pairing `OtherCreatureYouControl.ron`/`CreatureOpponentControls.ron`
// already use.
//
// Task 6 pilot addition, user-directed: exercises `HoleClass::FieldSlice`
// from the side `target <Param(0)>` doesn't reach — the frame `<Param(0)>
// you control` claims the nominal's `complements` field (the frame's own
// "you control") and leaves the hole with `modifiers`+`head`, the mirror
// image of `target <Param(0)>` (frame claims `determiner`, hole takes the
// rest).
//
// This did NOT compile as originally authored in this round: `classify()`
// (`crates/deckmaste_frames/src/compile.rs`) then only supported the
// determiner-owning shape. The finding was escalated, and the user ruled to
// reopen Task 4 and generalize `classify()`'s field-slice decision to a
// `(determiner, modifiers, complements)` occupancy table — the fix landed
// in this round (see `field_slice()` in `compile.rs`) — so this frame now
// compiles, the hole claiming `["modifiers", "head"]`. See
// `docs/superpowers/research/2026-07-30-macro-frames/
// pilot-constituency-findings.md` for the resolved finding, the new
// decision table, and the one further shape (a `modifiers`-only frame, e.g.
// `white <Param(0)>`) the user considered generalizing to and declined.
//
// Named distinctly from the existing `Condition`-kind `YouControl`
// (`plugins/builtin/macros/condition/YouControl.ron`, "you control ${0}",
// prenominal, unrelated body `Exists(And([Param(0), ControlledBy(Ref(You))]))`)
// even though `macro_ron::MacroSet` namespaces macro names by kind and the
// two would not collide at the engine level (`macros: HashMap<Ident /*kind*/,
// HashMap<Ident /*name*/, MacroDef>>`, `crates/macro_ron/src/set.rs:374`,
// `register`/`check_kinds` never compares across kinds). The reason to avoid
// reusing the name anyway: `cargo xtask macro inspect` resolves by name
// alone across every loaded macro (`plugin.macros.iter().find(|(_, def)|
// def.name.as_str() == name)`, `crates/xtask/src/macros/inspect.rs:136-139`)
// with no kind disambiguation, so two same-named macros in different kinds
// make `macro inspect` non-deterministic about which one it reports — a
// pre-existing latent hazard in this corpus (`Draw`/`Draws` already share
// names across `EventFilter` and `OneShotEffect`+`KeywordAction`, and
// `Creature` across `Predicate` and `TypeDef`) that a fresh macro shouldn't
// add another instance of.
(
    name: "ControlledByYou",
    template: "${0} you control",
    kinds: [Predicate],
    params: [Predicate],
    frames: ["<Param(0)> you control"],
    body: And([Param(0), ControlledBy(Ref(You))]),
)
